{"content_hash": "24f7777c5540c010", "version_id": 508, "article_id": 51, "level_code": "ja_n3", "lang": "ja", "level": 3, "level_label": "N3 中級", "title": "AI悪用と核戦争、2100年までに人類滅亡の恐れ ランセット委員会が警告", "title_zh": "AI滥用和核战争或致人类在2100年前灭绝，柳叶刀委员会警告", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/oct/11/nuclear-war-and-malicious-use-of-ai-threaten-end-of-humanity-by-2100-says-lancet-assessment", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1729284045177-7a40238e4cd0?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8NHx8bnVjbGVhciUyMHdhciUyMG1hbGljaW91c3xlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNjc3ODg3fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Emanuel Kypreos on Unsplash", "author": "Emanuel Kypreos", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@mankip67?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-large-cloud-of-smoke-is-billowing-out-of-the-sky-XySaPZljJ54?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(260, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(298, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "6a7c012390e8"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-10", "word_count": 215, "reading_minutes": 0.7, "lead": "医学雑誌ランセットの新しい委員会は、AIの悪用や核戦争など17の深刻な脅威を挙げました。人類が2100年までに滅びる可能性もあると言いますが、対策の道はあると強調しています。", "lead_zh": "医学杂志《柳叶刀》的新委员会列出了AI滥用、核战争等17项严重威胁。他们表示人类有可能在2100年前灭绝，但强调仍有应对之路。", "preview": "ランセットの委員会によると、AIの悪用や核戦争で人類が2100年までに絶滅する恐れがあります。これは17の健康への大きな脅威のリストの上位です。気候危機や子供の栄養不足、援助の削減なども入っています。", "preview_zh": "据《柳叶刀》委员会称，AI滥用和核战争可能导致人类在2100年前灭绝。这位列17项健康重大威胁之首。气候危机、儿童营养不良和援助削减等也在其中。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 496, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/51/ja_n3.mp3", "duration": 46.7, "size_bytes": 283968, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 144, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/508.json", "paragraphs": ["ランセットの委員会によると、AIの悪用や核戦争で人類が2100年までに絶滅する恐れがあります。これは17の健康への大きな脅威のリストの上位です。気候危機や子供の栄養不足、援助の削減なども入っています。", "専門家は、これらの脅威はお互いに関係しているので、一緒に対策する必要があると言います。でも、それぞれに「実行できる現実的な道」があると強調しました。今日の指導者の決定が次の世代の健康を形作るからです。", "報告書は、AIによる生物兵器や核戦争が絶滅のリスクを運ぶと述べています。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["据《柳叶刀》委员会称，AI滥用和核战争可能导致人类在2100年前灭绝。这位列17项健康重大威胁之首。气候危机、儿童营养不良和援助削减等也在其中。", "专家表示，这些威胁相互关联，因此需要共同应对。但他们强调，每一项都有“可付诸行动的现实路径”。因为今天领导人的决定将塑造下一代的健康。", "报告指出，AI生物武器和核战争带来灭绝风险。可能性虽低，但一旦发生将给人类带来巨大灾难。粒子进入大气层遮挡阳光，可能引发饥荒。"], "body": "ランセットの委員会によると、AIの悪用や核戦争で人類が2100年までに絶滅する恐れがあります。これは17の健康への大きな脅威のリストの上位です。気候危機や子供の栄養不足、援助の削減なども入っています。\n\n専門家は、これらの脅威はお互いに関係しているので、一緒に対策する必要があると言います。でも、それぞれに「実行できる現実的な道」があると強調しました。今日の指導者の決定が次の世代の健康を形作るからです。\n\n報告書は、AIによる生物兵器や核戦争が絶滅のリスクを運ぶと述べています。", "body_zh": "据《柳叶刀》委员会称，AI滥用和核战争可能导致人类在2100年前灭绝。这位列17项健康重大威胁之首。气候危机、儿童营养不良和援助削减等也在其中。\n\n专家表示，这些威胁相互关联，因此需要共同应对。但他们强调，每一项都有“可付诸行动的现实路径”。因为今天领导人的决定将塑造下一代的健康。\n\n报告指出，AI生物武器和核战争带来灭绝风险。可能性虽低，但一旦发生将给人类带来巨大灾难。粒子进入大气层遮挡阳光，可能引发饥荒。", "text": "ランセットの委員会によると、AIの悪用や核戦争で人類が2100年までに絶滅する恐れがあります。これは17の健康への大きな脅威のリストの上位です。気候危機や子供の栄養不足、援助の削減なども入っています。 専門家は、これらの脅威はお互いに関係しているので、一緒に対策する必要があると言います。でも、それぞれに「実行できる現実的な道」があると強調しました。今日の指導者の決定が次の世代の健康を形作るからです。 報告書は、AIによる生物兵器や核戦争が絶滅のリスクを運ぶと述べています。", "vocab": [{"word": "悪用", "pos": "noun", "zh": "滥用", "note": "常与「AIの悪用」搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "脅威", "pos": "noun", "zh": "威胁", "note": "指危险的事物", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "絶滅", "pos": "noun", "zh": "灭绝", "note": "如「人類の絶滅」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "委員会", "pos": "noun", "zh": "委员会", "note": "专家组成的组织", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "栄養不足", "pos": "noun", "zh": "营养不良", "note": "如「子供の栄養不足」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "削減", "pos": "noun", "zh": "削减", "note": "如「援助の削減」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "対策", "pos": "noun", "zh": "对策", "note": "如「対策を取る」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "強調する", "pos": "verb", "zh": "强调", "note": "如「強調しました」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "リスク", "pos": "noun", "zh": "风险", "note": "外来语", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "飢饉", "pos": "noun", "zh": "饥荒", "note": "粮食严重不足", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "医療制度", "pos": "noun", "zh": "医疗制度", "note": "如「医療制度の強化」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "指導者", "pos": "noun", "zh": "领导人", "note": "如「指導者の決定」", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Nuclear war and malicious use of AI threaten end of humanity by 2100, says Lancet assessment", "summary_original": "Newly established commission identifies 17 catastrophic threats to human health but says ‘realistic route to act’ on each exists\nHumans could become extinct by the year 2100 due to malicious use of AI or nuclear conflict, according to a new global risk assessment.\nThey top a list of 17 major threats to human health over the next 75 years, which also includes cuts to aid spending by wealthy countries, the climate crisis and childhood malnutrition.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Nuclear war and malicious use of AI threaten end of humanity by 2100, says Lancet assessment\nNewly established commission identifies 17 catastrophic threats to human health but says ‘realistic route to act’ on each exists\nHumans could become extinct by the year 2100 due to malicious use of AI or nuclear conflict, according to a new global risk assessment.\nThey top a list of 17 major threats to human health over the next 75 years, which also includes cuts to aid spending by wealthy countries, the climate crisis and childhood malnutrition.\nThe experts behind\nThe Lancet Commission on 21st Century Global Threats to Health\nsaid all the threats interact, meaning they must be addressed together – but stressed that there was “a realistic route to act” on each.\n“Decisions made by leaders today will shape the health and wellbeing of the next generation,” said Prof Christopher Murray, commission co-chair and the director of the Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation, University of Washington.\nTo create its list, the commission modelled how many years in good health might be lost due to sickness, disability or early deaths due to each threat, based on current trajectories – a measure known as disability-adjusted life years (Dalys).\n“Malicious use of AI, including bioweapons, and nuclear conflict with nuclear famine carry risks of extinction in the next 75 years,” the report said, adding that while their likelihood remained low, they had the potential to end humanity in the case of nuclear conflict by injecting enough particles into the upper atmosphere to block sunlight and cause famine, or via AI-created biological weapons. An accompanying Lancet editorial, published alongside the report, warned: “The scale of harm, should they be realised, would inflict an apocalypse on humanity.”\nOther risks that could cause more than 1bn cumulative Dalys, and therefore deemed “major catastrophic threats”, included\nair pollution\n,\nantimicrobial resistance\n,\nchildhood malnutrition\nand climate breakdown, as well as conventional conflict,\ndeclining overseas aid\n,\nhigh alcohol use\n, high blood pressure, income inequality, low educational attainment,\nnaturally occurring pandemics\n,\nobesity\n, poor\nmental health\n,\nsmoking\nand unhealthy\nageing\n.\nTo be included on the list, threats not only had to potentially cause a high number of lost healthy years, but also to have potential solutions.\nIbrahim Abubakar, commission member and professor of infectious disease epidemiology at UCL, said: “We are not starting from a point of view of ‘oh look, we want to scare you – we’ve got X many threats facing humanity’. We’re starting from the premise that if you are a policymaker today, whether at the global multilateral level or at the national level, these are the potential threats that you could face, and this is the magnitude by which, if you act, you can actually make a difference.”\nAction to limit\nglobal heating to about 1.8C (3.2F)\nrather than letting it reach 4.4C could prevent 1.89bn years of healthy life being lost, according to the report, which modelled best and worst case scenarios for each threat.\nIn higher income regions, non-communicable diseases such as obesity and poor mental health were the dominant threats, while in lower income regions health loss was driven by issues such as low educational attainment.\nMany major donor nations, including the US and UK, have announced\nlarge cuts to aid spending\nover the past year. The potential collapse of, or steep reduction in, international health aid could cause up to 1.5bn Dalys before 2100, the commission found, nearly 70% of which would be in sub-Saharan Africa. The region also bears the brunt of child malnutrition.\nThe commission was made up of 35 experts, and its findings will be shared on Sunday at the World Health Summit in Berlin, Germany. Their assessment will be updated annually to re-evaluate the 17 threats identified, incorporating new data and any emerging hazards.\nThe authors urged leaders to address the risks before they escalated into crises, including via investment in technological innovations and by strengthening health systems.\n“We started this process three years ago, thinking that there were three big threats: conflict, climate, and pandemics,” said Murray. “There’s a much larger number of threats that we need to worry about, and governments really need to dedicate some money and staff to the task of anticipation, prevention and preparation for this more diverse set of threats.”\nExplore more on these topics\nGlobal health\nAI (artificial intelligence)\nNuclear weapons\nClimate crisis\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-11T00:18:05.945804", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "ランセット", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.775, "sm": 125, "em": 775, "cs": 0, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "の", "s": 0.787, "e": 0.925, "sm": 787, "em": 925, "cs": 5, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "委員会", "s": 0.938, "e": 1.5, "sm": 937, "em": 1500